# Drafted by Gemini (R26 White Worm), edited. The White Worm: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_worm_arrived
Narrator: A lakeside village of grey huts, nets draped on every post, and white worms gleaming in the shallows.
check Wisdom DC 17 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep your mind on the names of those you love and the water's whisper slides off.
set mf_worm_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A hero breathes the lake's mist and loses a quarter hour entirely; they come back with a headache and no memory of why.
damage 2d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk the shore, and the lake mist drifts into your mouth with a taste of cold pennies.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 17 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_pell_fisher [afraid]: He says the nets come up full of white worms, and the water makes a man forget his own children's names.
set mf_worm_asked
quest mf_worm asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_pell_fisher [weary]: He says another family lost their memory in the shallows this morning, and asks for news.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_worm_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_pell_fisher [afraid]: Drink from the lake and you forget everything for hours; swim and the worms get in under your skin; and the lake cultists say they hear it singing.
-> menu

~ where
mf_pell_fisher [sad]: He says it was something pulled through from another place by a woman called Matron Lethica, and it fell into the deep lake.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_pell_fisher [neutral]: He says the first people of the lake left black obelisks on the shore; they might tell what lies in the water, if someone could read them.
* [Arcana DC 17] Decipher the black obelisks -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Investigation DC 17] Study the lake's first people's carvings -> a_ok | a_slow
* Copy every carving and puzzle at them for hours -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_pell_fisher [smile]: The carvings are a warning, plain once you see it, and a map of the rift where the thing came through.
time +60
set mf_worm_found
set mf_worm_clue_a
quest mf_worm trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You spend a long afternoon copying the obelisks onto your sleeves, and by evening the pattern at last makes sense.
time +300
set mf_worm_found
quest mf_worm trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: He greets you like old friends and asks if you have heard the Worm singing under the lake, and would you like to join the choir.
set mf_worm_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_lake_cultist [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_worm_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_worm_found and not flag.mf_worm_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: He says the Worm eats minds and the faithful are those it has already tasted; the choir meets on the long jetty each midnight.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: He says the Order is always glad of new voices; you would only have to pretend to love the Worm convincingly.
* [Deception DC 17] Pretend to join the Worm's order -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Persuasion DC 17] Talk the cultists into taking you to the rift -> b_ok | b_slow
* Sit through the whole sermon and follow them out -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: Brother Silt weeps with joy, and the choir leads you down the jetty to the rift.
time +60
set mf_worm_found
set mf_worm_clue_b
quest mf_worm trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It is an unpleasantly long sermon, but the choir does at last walk you down the jetty to the rift.
time +300
set mf_worm_found
quest mf_worm trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: He whispers that the Worm fears one star pattern, the ones the lake's first people painted; show it that sequence and it will choke on whoever knows it.
* [Arcana DC 17] Work out the constellations from the obelisks -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Nature DC 17] Chart the stars by the lake's reflection -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Trace the whole sky on the shore, star by star -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: You mark the seven stars in order on a scrap of oilcloth, and the lake seems to flinch from it.
time +60
give mf_star_chart
set mf_worm_weak
quest mf_worm ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes the whole night, lying on the shore with a lamp, but the chart is finished by dawn.
time +300
give mf_star_chart
set mf_worm_weak
quest mf_worm ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: Down the long jetty a tear in the air hangs open over black water, and a white shape coils beyond it.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_worm_reveals
Narrator: The White Worm rises, vast and pale, from the rift in the lake bed, its mouth a ring of soft teeth.
cutscene mf_worm_reveals_2
Narrator: It sings, and every worm in the water turns toward you at once.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_worm_weak
combat mf_worm_weak
elif level >= 14
combat mf_worm_full
else
combat mf_worm_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_worm_falls
Narrator: The Worm shudders, coils tight, and falls back through the rift, which closes on it like a wound.
cutscene mf_worm_falls_2
Narrator: The moon swings its gaze over the water toward a dark forest to the north.
cutscene end
set mf_worm_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give eye_of_the_white_worm
quest mf_worm slain
xp milestone
Narrator: In Hartsblight, the trees are already bending their heads toward something tall.
-> END
